Attribution — Status Trio design inspiration

The taskbar system-status icon (battery ring, Wi-Fi glyph, and volume dots in
one tile, backed by SystemStatusService sampling public IOKit, CoreWLAN,
CoreAudio, and IOBluetooth APIs) is an original, clean-room implementation
inspired by the design of Status Trio by lingyired
(https://github.com/lingyired/status-trio), which is licensed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0. No Status Trio source code is included in this project.

The external-display brightness path follows the IOAVService I2C interface
shape used by Status Trio's DDCPrivateAPI module, which itself carries the
MIT-licensed AppleSiliconDDC notice (Copyright (c) 2021 Istvan T.). The
implementation here is original; only the interface shape and the MIT
attribution pattern were studied. No third-party source code is included.

The taskbar strip composition (divider-as-data items with orphan pruning),
per-display filtering discipline, and settings-driven preview discipline follow
patterns studied from eskele by hossainalhaidari
(https://github.com/hossainalhaidari/eskele), MIT licensed. The implementation
here is original; no eskele source code is included.
